sequenceDiagram
  participant M as Trusted OCC management
  participant C as OCC authority
  participant L as Refresh owner
  participant F as Forwarder
  participant P as Provider
  Note over M,P: Proposed flow, logical contracts do not require separate daemons
  M->>C: Authenticate caller / user and exact preparation purpose
  C-->>M: Preparation Permit or refusal
  break Denied or authority unavailable
    Note over M,C: Refuse before material access
  end
  M->>L: prepare(Preparation, Command)
  Note over M,L: Same fenced owner, owner authorizes issuer I/O<br/>Agent / bootstrap cannot select preparation
  L-->>M: Change of LifecycleStatus
  break Failed, uncertain, withdrawn or too late
    Note over M,L: Preserve operation and cleanup, inspect / reconcile, no blind replay
  end
  M->>F: capture authenticated business operation, forward
  F->>C: EgressAuthorizer.check(before_access)
  C-->>F: AccessPermit or Refusal
  F->>F: CredentialResolver.resolve via readWarm<br/>No request-path issuance
  F->>C: EgressAuthorizer.check(before_send)<br/>Actual operation + MaterialEvidence
  C-->>F: SendPermit or Refusal
  alt Both checks allow and material usable within original deadline
    F->>P: Inject and send once
    P-->>F: Provider response
    F->>F: Apply registered response policy
    F-->>M: SafeResponse or blocked / uncertain outcome
    M->>M: Return sanitized metadata only
  else Denied, unavailable, unusable or too late
    F-->>M: Refuse before dispatch
  end
  Note over M,P: Roots stay with owner / issuer, no tokens or handles to Agent / UI<br/>No automatic retry after possible dispatch
